The thing is, answering naicai does not mean "absolutely not, and I =20
shall that you never to mention it in my presence again".  It only =20
says "absolutely not"

You might infer anger, but for that you'd need to add some other =20
attitudinals.

If you said "cai" that would mean "absolutely" - the event is funny.

You could add je'unai to mark that you don't really mean the cai, but =20=

that's kind of like quoting.

I guess sarcasm doesn't go so well in a language that is supposed to =20
be unambiguous. Humor, sarcasm, and irony. They all seem to depend on =20=

ambiguities.

mu'o mi'e ioAV

